    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1322,
      "versionNonce": 277572837,
      "index": "b50",
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "nirYHiq-jJSolK6rTtbtg",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 970.6428571428571,
      "y": 590.2500000000003,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 575.8179146902903,
      "height": 725,
      "seed": 1801317563,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [
        {
          "id": "3mfSj-_tH89a3D5WNhJh7",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1727084901042,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "Modelling\n1. Model selection (LR,GBT,SVM,DT,NN,etc)\n    * simple baseline - can be rule based\n    * simple model - such as LR\n    * switch to complex model\n    * ensemble models\n    * others: data size, speed, hyper param tunning, \ncontinuous training, interpretability, etc\n2. Training\n    * dataset (raw, fe&labels, sampling strategy, split)\n    * imbalance label - down/up sampling, class balanced \nloss, focal loss\n    * from scratch vs fine tuning\n    * distributed training (multi GPU)\n3. Others\n    * inference latency, interpretability, device/cloud, cont. \ntraining\n    * number of params, memory req. \n    * NN structure - ResNet, Transformer, number of \nhidden layers, number of neurons, activation function\n\n    * loss function - MSE MAE CE SoftMax HuberLoss\n    * regularization - L1 L2 CV Dropout\n    * Optimization - SGD Adam Momentum RMSProp\n    * Activation - ReLU Tanh SigMoid\n    * Bias-Variance tradeoff\n    * Over/under fitting and solution\n    * continual training - train on each new data, \npersonalize the model to each user, how often to retrain",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Modelling\n1. Model selection (LR,GBT,SVM,DT,NN,etc)\n    * simple baseline - can be rule based\n    * simple model - such as LR\n    * switch to complex model\n    * ensemble models\n    * others: data size, speed, hyper param tunning, continuous training, interpretability, etc\n2. Training\n    * dataset (raw, fe&labels, sampling strategy, split)\n    * imbalance label - down/up sampling, class balanced loss, focal loss\n    * from scratch vs fine tuning\n    * distributed training (multi GPU)\n3. Others\n    * inference latency, interpretability, device/cloud, cont. training\n    * number of params, memory req. \n    * NN structure - ResNet, Transformer, number of hidden layers, number of neurons, activation function\n\n    * loss function - MSE MAE CE SoftMax HuberLoss\n    * regularization - L1 L2 CV Dropout\n    * Optimization - SGD Adam Momentum RMSProp\n    * Activation - ReLU Tanh SigMoid\n    * Bias-Variance tradeoff\n    * Over/under fitting and solution\n    * continual training - train on each new data, personalize the model to each user, how often to retrain",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
