        {
          "id": "9FZUKn_UcQX133tRLG3gW",
          "type": "arrow"
        }
      ],
      "updated": 1727084901042,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "Visual Search\n\nModelling\n1. Use NN - good at handling unstructured data\n    - need embeddings to compute similarity\n2. Models\n    - ResNet, Residual Neural Network\n    - ViT: Vision Transformer\n    - Hyper parameters: #conv, #fullconn, emb size, etc\n3. Training\n    - Contrastive training:  ( [emb, emb1, emb2, ..., embN], Label(1-N) )\n    - Construct training data: randomly choose query image, and n-1 negative\n    - Positive label: human annotation, from interaction, autogen from query\n        * human annotation is costly and time consuming\n        * from interaction: noisy, may have a lot of data missing labels\n        * autogen: insufficient representing of real world\n        * approach: SimCLR -> interaction -> human\n    - Choose Loss: SoftMax, CE\n        * Compute similarities: dot product, cosine similarity, Euclidean distance(curse of dim)\n        * SoftMax\n        * Cross Entropy\n    - Pre trained model\n        * how to fine tune\n",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Visual Search\n\nModelling\n1. Use NN - good at handling unstructured data\n    - need embeddings to compute similarity\n2. Models\n    - ResNet, Residual Neural Network\n    - ViT: Vision Transformer\n    - Hyper parameters: #conv, #fullconn, emb size, etc\n3. Training\n    - Contrastive training:  ( [emb, emb1, emb2, ..., embN], Label(1-N) )\n    - Construct training data: randomly choose query image, and n-1 negative\n    - Positive label: human annotation, from interaction, autogen from query\n        * human annotation is costly and time consuming\n        * from interaction: noisy, may have a lot of data missing labels\n        * autogen: insufficient representing of real world\n        * approach: SimCLR -> interaction -> human\n    - Choose Loss: SoftMax, CE\n        * Compute similarities: dot product, cosine similarity, Euclidean distance(curse of dim)\n        * SoftMax\n        * Cross Entropy\n    - Pre trained model\n        * how to fine tune\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
